			<div class="content" id="post-content-4569030">
									

<p>As it says in the summary, I thought in these boring times it would be cool to share our favorite films, tv series, books, video games and what have you that despite being great, don't have huge exposure.</p>
<p><strong>Movies:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Absentia: Mike Flanagans first horror movie. Legitimately unsettling</li>
<li>Woman in black: Harry potter has to do paperwork with a nasty ghost lady.</li>
<li>Ironclad: Fictionalised account of the siege of a castle in England featuring really good acting and vikings getting cut in half.</li>
<li>Wolf Creek: Huge here in Aus, but I dunno if it got big overseas. Three friends on holiday get caught by a nasty serial killer.</li>
<li>Rogue: People trapped on an island by a crocodile</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Tv Shows:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Deadwood: About the goings on in a wild west gold mining town.</li>
<li>Carnivale: Mystical goings on surrounding a travelling circs in the great depression, involving a battle between avatars of good and evil, a ghost town, and friendship.</li>
<li>Penny Dreadful: Kind of like the leagueo extraordinary gentlemen if it was done well. should be much more popular</li>
</ul>

