			<div class="content" id="post-content-4569789">
									

<p>I'll just add mine.</p>
<p><strong>Movies</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>I, Robot: In the distant future, a cop who has a dark history with robots, investigates an alleged suicide of a famous scientist. Only to find himself in a much deeper mystery. It might just be the nostalgia talking but I think it's a fun to watch movie. For a 2004 film, the CGI was pretty great.</li>
<li>Zathura: Though it might be well known, I really feel like it's a bit underrated. It may be a spinoff of Jumanji but the whole plot set in space seems so bizarre and weird that I feel like it only scratched the surface of what the game can do.</li>
<li>Spider-Man 2: Again, well known and nostalgia factor but it is was it is.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Book/s</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>I Am Number Four series: Though used solely for my school Book Report, I think a spinoff comic/manga can be a great fresh look. The whole story of super powered human(oid) aliens fighting high tech human(oid) aliens is cliche but a spinoff would be nice.</li>
<li>House of Scorpion/Lord of Opium: Again, a school Book Report, but I feel like the whole setting could use some illustrations. A story set in a sci-fi world about a boy, genetically cloned to be an exact copy of a drug lord, get his life changed when he finally knows the truth. Pretty decent read I should say, though I can't say for the ending of the second book.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>TV show/s</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Berserk 2016/2017: Here me out, I know the use of CGI in this Godly-made manga ruins the whole look and tone but I'm just glad they managed to animate it (though it still looks like shit).</li>
<li>Mairimashita! Iruma-kun: Slice of life, shonen, and school type of anime. Wholesome and bizarre but really great. (If you want to see Blue Haired Midoriya then watch this one)</li>
<li>Punisher (Netflix): It has what Punisher is, a broken man escaping from a traumatic experience with what only he knows best to do. The whole show (only watched the first season) provides a great look on what the Punisher can do with his capabilities. Even when you know that he's gonna exact revenge, you just expect it to be painful and brutal. Though he has a slight bloodlust in his mind, the show provides some humanity to him.</li>
</ul>

