			<div class="content" id="post-content-4676442">
									

<p>As far as movies go, I think the least appreciated film of the past decade is Sion Sono's Love &amp; Peace. It's a Japanese tokusatsu (basically live action with an emphasis on special effects) film about love, punk rock, introversion, christmas spirit, and a giant turtle. If you can track down a way to watch it, it's one of the most uniquely heartwarming stories ever put to film.</p>
<p>Others I'd have to list:<br />
Senna (directed by Asif Kapadia), an amazing documentary about the incredible life of a Brazilian racecar driver comprised almost entirely of archival footage with no voice over.<br />
Colossal (directed by Nacho Vigalondo), a film about childhood memories and giant monsters fighting robots.<br />
Dead Silence (directed by James Wan), a horror film with a slick as hell aesthetic and fantastic atmosphere.<br />
and Wrong (directed by Quentin Dupieux), a surreal odyssey following a nervous wreck who just wants to find his lost dog.</p>

