			<div class="content" id="post-content-4706196">
									

<p>I'm not that much of a movie watcher coz i got bored watching movies or tvs years ago, but i am a reader. There is this novel that I've read and i already finished it and i really love it. This is the first time that a novel got me thinking &quot;I want to read this forever&quot;. It may be an exaggeration but that's what i feel for it coz i really love it and i hope more people will read it.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Omniscient Reader's Viewpoint</strong> it is about a novel reader. His favorite novel became a reality but unfortunately it is an apocalyptic story so yeah he has to work on how to survive. It has a tragedy tag so be prepared for a roller coaster of emotions. It gave me existential crisis at the end hahaha.</li>
</ul>
<p>At first i was going to skip this novel coz i got bored of the cliche stories where you need to kill people to survive the game. You know, the stories where there is some mysterious guy and there are people being held against their will and they need to kill each other to survive. But i decided to give it a chance and boy am i glad that i did! ORV is not the typical/cliche survival novels. There are so many twists along the way that i very much like. The fighting scenes too is so epic. It maybe just me overreacting but the love i have for this novel is great, and i want other people to see it too.</p>
<p>Oh it has a manhwa now with the same title. For the people who doesn't read novels XD</p>
<p>Edit: i forgot, if you like historical, heroes(not super hero, i mean historical heroes XD), mythologies&#8230; ORV also have some in there.</p>

