<p>Before giving my own recommendations, I want to signal-boost some of the previously mentioned gems.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>Absentia</em> (maybe it's because I went into it not expecting much, but it was the most engrossing movie I'd ever watched)</p>
<p><em>First four horror movies Professor_JD mentioned</em></p>
<p><em>Virus</em> (very enjoyable movie and has one of my favorite movie monsters)</p>
<p><em>9</em> and <em>Django Unchained</em> (good movies that I need to fully watch)</p>
<p><em>Property of Hate</em> (I gotta catch up on this one)</p>
<p><em>Kill Six Billion Demons</em> (beautiful/amazing/marvelous)</p>
<p><em>Blasphemous</em> (fun game with a fascinating aesthetic)</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Movies</strong></p>
<p><strong>Errementari: The Devil and the Blacksmith</strong> - A very fun and charming movie about an orphan girl, a demon, and a sad blacksmith.</p>
<p><strong>Leviathan (1989 Film)</strong> - Not really a hidden gem cause it's not super good, it's like a worse version of Virus. The monster is neat though; I really want to see it as the subject of a kaiju movie.</p>
<p><strong>Phantoms</strong> - Two sisters take a trip to a town, but all its residents have mysteriously disappeared. If you've ever seen Prince of Darkness, this is a better version of it imo.</p>
<p><strong>From Beyond</strong> - I love this movie, it's brilliantly goofy.</p>
<p><strong>AM1200</strong> - 40 minute cosmic horror film. Extremely underrated.</p>
<p><strong>The Dark (2018 Film)</strong> - A teen film about a murderous ghoul girl and a scarred blind boy. I feel like it was made by (and for) fans of creepypasta characters ala Jeff/Jane the Killer, Clockwork, Ticci Toby, etc.<br />
&#8230;I liked it.</p>
<p><strong>The Endless</strong> - I don't know if it's underexposed, but it's a great cosmic horror buddy comedy.</p>

